  "caveats": [
    "The published RMSE is RMSE_mean - the mean of per-day RMSEs - which is what the manuscript states. pooled_RMSE in the same file is over observations and is consistently higher; the two are not interchangeable.",
    "Madrigal rows carry the madrigal_reference_offset caveat.",
    "Tables 3/4 report RMSE/MAE/R2 with across-day median and quartiles (RMSE_median/RMSE_q1/RMSE_q3), not mean +/- std - the day distribution is skewed and mean +/- std implies a symmetry it does not have. The _mean/_std columns are kept so nothing already published moves. AbsErr_p95_median/AbsErr_p99_median are the across-day median of each day's own absolute-error percentile, not a pooled percentile over all observations."
